# Build context for every image in this repository. The context is the repository root
# (the NSwag tool manifest lives in .config/ and the generation script in scripts/, both
# outside src/), so this file has to keep the large and the misleading out of it.
#
# "Misleading" is the important half. Docker sends gitignored files that happen to exist on
# disk, so a developer's locally-generated API client would be copied into the image and the
# build would appear to succeed on a machine where a clean checkout fails. The generated
# clients and the client bundle are therefore excluded here on purpose: every image build
# regenerates them.

# Version control and editor state
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/*.*proj.user

# Build output
**/bin
**/obj
**/dist
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
src/FantasyCritic.ClientAppVue2/src/api/generated
src/FantasyCritic.ApiClient/Generated

# Test fixtures: ~135 MB of LFS-backed CSVs that no image runs.
src/FantasyCritic.Test/TestData

# Not part of any image
**/.env
**/azds.yaml
**/charts
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
**/Dockerfile*
**/docker-compose*
.cursor
.github
deploy
docs
infrastructure
LICENSE
README.md
